haplo-dialog — Announcements for users
======================================

This file summarises the important changes from the user's point of view.
For the complete technical history, see CHANGELOG.md.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Version 1.1.0 (in preparation)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

* The XML test suite goes from 20 to 50 test cases.

* Auto-detection of the graphical environment (terminal and editor) and
  command allowlist broadened to other package managers.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Version 1.0.0 (2026-05-29) — First public release
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

haplo-dialog 1.0.0 is the first stable public release: gtk3dialog, the
port of gtkdialog 0.8.3 onto GTK3.

* gtkdialog compatibility: the package provides gtkdialog (symbolic link). A
  single binary answers to both names, gtkdialog and gtk3dialog — your legacy
  gtkdialog scripts run as is.

* gtkdialog's XML syntax is kept identical.

* Strengthened security: all commands go through safe_system().
  No more direct calls to system() in the code.

* Binary hardening: FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO, NX stack,
  stack canary.

* Packaging for Debian, Fedora, Arch, Gentoo, Slackware.

To install:

  # Debian / Ubuntu / Haplo-Linux
  sudo apt install gtk3dialog

  # From source
  cd gtk3dialog/gtk3dialog_1.0.0 && ./configure && make && sudo make install

Documentation: https://haplo-dialog.fr
Bug reports: devel@haplo-dialog.fr
Security: devel@haplo-dialog.fr

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
